-## Subtopics
-
-### Gaussian Allocation Policy
-A learned policy that distributes the Gaussian budget $B$ across anchors based on local scene significance (e.g., texture complexity). It differs from uniform allocation by concentrating capacity in high-frequency regions. Choose this when you need adaptive resource distribution. [Link to [Gaussian Allocation Policy](16746-feed-forward-generalizable-reconstruction.md#gaussian-allocation-policy)] (Note: Specific sub-article not provided in tree, linked to parent context).
-
-### Resource-Linear Decoder
-A decoder that refines Gaussians via local cross-attention with hierarchical neighbor search, ensuring $O(B \cdot K_{gs})$ complexity. Choose this when you need inference cost to scale linearly with $B$. [Link to [Resource-Linear Decoder](16746-feed-forward-generalizable-reconstruction.md#resource-linear-decoder)] (Note: Specific sub-article not provided in tree, linked to parent context).
+*   **Training Failure:** Removing the projection loss causes training to fail entirely, as it ties anchor Gaussians to the image region they were encoded from [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Neighbor Search Accuracy:** Removing the Voronoi loss causes a significant PSNR drop (2.51 dB) because Gaussians leave their anchor's cell, and the hierarchical search no longer retrieves their true neighbors [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Local Refinement:** Removing the local refinement module lowers PSNR by 0.96 dB, as Gaussians cannot be made consistent with neighbors [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The decoding cost is $O(B \cdot K_{gs})$, scaling linearly with the Gaussian budget $B$, compared to global self-attention which costs $O(B^2)$ [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Decoding cost is $O(B \cdot K_{gs})$, scaling linearly with the Gaussian budget $B$ [S1, unofficial]. This contrasts with global self-attention, which costs $O(B^2)$ [S1, unofficial].
